---
import { shot } from '../../data/shots';
import movesMp4 from '../../assets/clips/moves.mp4?url';
import movesWebm from '../../assets/clips/moves.webm?url';
import movesPoster from '../../assets/clips/moves.webp';
import Clip from '../media/Clip.astro';
import Shot from '../media/Shot.astro';
import Chapter from './Chapter.astro';
import Frame from './Frame.astro';
---

<Chapter title="Start knows where everything is.">
	<p>
		Type a few letters and Start finds apps, settings, files and even the words inside them. It does sums and unit
		conversions, and turns on dark style or Wi-Fi when you ask.
	</p>
	<Frame slot="media">
		<Shot {...shot('search')} alt="Start searching for dark, with the dark style action and matching settings" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 48rem, (min-width: 48rem) 64vw, 94vw" />
	</Frame>
</Chapter>

<Chapter title="The essentials, one click away." flip>
	<p>
		Quick settings are tiles you arrange yourself. Notifications group by app, with replies, media controls and a
		calendar right next to them.
	</p>
	<div slot="media" class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:gap-6">
		<Frame>
			<Shot {...shot('quick')} alt="Quick settings with network, power mode, dark style and volume" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 24rem, (min-width: 48rem) 32vw, 47vw" />
		</Frame>
		<Frame class="translate-y-10">
			<Shot {...shot('notifications')} alt="The notification center with a calendar" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 24rem, (min-width: 48rem) 32vw, 47vw" />
		</Frame>
	</div>
</Chapter>

<Chapter title="Room for every window.">
	<p>
		Snap windows into layouts or see them all at once. Or turn any desktop into a board, an endless canvas where
		windows sit side by side and you zoom out to see the whole picture.
	</p>
	<div slot="media" class="space-y-4 md:space-y-6">
		<Frame>
			<Shot {...shot('board')} alt="A desktop as a board, with every window side by side" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 48rem, (min-width: 48rem) 64vw, 94vw" />
		</Frame>
		<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:gap-6">
			<Frame>
				<Shot {...shot('snap')} alt="Snap layouts for the focused window" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 24rem, (min-width: 48rem) 32vw, 47vw" />
			</Frame>
			<Frame>
				<Shot {...shot('tasks')} alt="Every window and desktop at a glance" sizes="(min-width: 76rem) 24rem, (min-width: 48rem) 32vw, 47vw" />
			</Frame>
		</div>
	</div>
</Chapter>

<Chapter title="It moves like it means it." flip>
	<p>
		Everything in Luft moves on springs, so it can change its mind halfway without a jolt. Swipes follow your fingers
		and land where you meant, and apps open quickly, even the first time.
	</p>
	<Frame slot="media">
		<Clip webm={movesWebm} mp4={movesMp4} poster={movesPoster} label="Start, quick settings, every window at a glance and the board, opening and closing in Luft" />
	</Frame>
</Chapter>
